31,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems that sitting close to one another has a wonderful effect! Our new joiners learned so much just by overhearing us, and the project strands worked much more smoothly when they were within earshot.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The costs are quite rigid. We are billed for the total area regardless of how many desks we use, and every single change to the power and network layout incurs a fee per desk.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found the same things. It's worrying that we're paying for empty space every month, and those fees for moving the power lines... they could really add up if we change our minds.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh wow, the pilot floor is a bit of a mess! It takes up to nine minutes just to get screens working every morning. And those unplanned shuffles? Two weeks of boxes and interruptions is way too long!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's exactly as I suspected. The noise levels by the printer are significantly higher, and the physio's notes confirm that getting a workstation actually comfortable takes days of tedious tweaking. We can't just treat desks like interchangeable tiles.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Toshio, @Daisuke, I understand the costs are a concern, but isn't the harmony and growth of our team worth a little investment? It would be a shame to prioritize the budget over our connection.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Investment is fine, but we must be realistic. If we make a decision based on harmony without considering the cost of changes, we risk a plan that is financially unsustainable or rejected by the department.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't want to be the one to bring everyone down, but the budget hasn't increased even though we have more people now. If we spend too much on changes, I'm afraid we'll have no room for error.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shizue, I agree that harmony is great, but imagine if we're all stressed because our mornings are a hassle! If it takes nearly ten minutes just to start working, that's a lot of wasted energy every single day.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, you're worried about ten minutes of setup, but I'm talking about eight hours of physical strain. If we ignore the noise and ergonomics, we're just choosing which kind of misery we prefer. Data doesn't lie; the printer area is a noise trap.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I understand everyone's worries. @Shunichi, your health is very important, and @Mio, I wouldn't want you to start your day feeling rushed. Perhaps there is a way to keep us close for that lovely teamwork while still being mindful of the noise and costs?","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"Regardless of the layout, some positions will inevitably be less desirable than others. We should be honest about who will end up in the noise trap or the less ergonomic spots before we finalize anything.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Toshio. If we pick a layout that's too expensive to change, we might be stuck in those bad spots forever. I just... I really hope we can find a way to be fair without overspending.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Daisuke, exactly! And @Shunichi, those ""days of tweaking"" you mentioned sound like a nightmare if we have to do it every time we move. We need a setup that's stable so we don't lose our precious time!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, for once we agree. Stability isn't just about your morning routine; it's about not having to spend a week fighting with a monitor arm every time someone decides they want a ""fresh perspective"" on the floor plan. We need a permanent solution.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"It sounds like we all want stability and fairness. Let's keep our hearts open to a solution that protects our health and budget, while still letting us lean on each other for support.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
