60,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I feel that Option A might be a bit too lonely, as we would lose those wonderful chance conversations that help our new joiners feel so welcome. I believe we need a way to stay connected.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A is impractical. Between the daily setup time Mio mentioned and the ergonomic issues Shunichi raised, it would be a disaster. Furthermore, it avoids the necessary conversation about who occupies the worst seats.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Toshio. Option A sounds like it would cause a lot of daily stress, and if we have to re-run power or network for a flexible setup, I'm worried about the cost.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A is a total no-go for me! If it takes nine minutes just to get screens working, doing that every single morning would eat up all my breaks. It sounds so exhausting!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option A is a joke. Expecting us to spend our days in a state of ergonomic chaos while fighting with cables just to ""be flexible"" is absurd. I'm voting against it with every fiber of my being.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"Option B seems very lovely because it gives us a stable home. If we group ourselves by function, we can keep those helpful project strands close together and ensure our new joiners always have someone to lean on.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is the most cost-effective since it minimizes the facilities charges for re-running power. However, it permanently assigns the worst seats. We must decide now how to handle those positions fairly, rather than ignoring the disparity.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Option B is the safest for the budget. Since we're already paying for empty space, we can't afford to keep paying for power changes. But... I'm worried about who gets the bad seats.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, @Daisuke, if Option B means we just set up once and stay put, that sounds like a dream! No more morning cable struggles and no more two-week shuffles. I'm totally okay with that stability!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Option B is the only rational choice here. If it takes days to settle into a workstation, rotating blocks in Option C is just a scheduled way to be uncomfortable. I'll take a ""bad"" seat over constant instability any day.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Toshio, @Daisuke, if we are worried about the bad seats, perhaps we can decide together who sits where with kindness and fairness? I believe Option B allows us to cherish our connections without the stress of moving.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Kindness is not a system. If we choose Option B, we must explicitly agree on who takes the noise trap and the poor ergonomics. I will not support a plan that leaves the worst spots to be filled by habit or silence.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't want anyone to feel like they're being forced into a bad spot. But if we choose Option C, the costs for re-running power every time we shift... I'm really afraid we can't afford that.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, I agree! We can just talk it out and decide together who goes where. As long as we don't have to move every few months or every single morning, I'm happy! Option B sounds so peaceful.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, you're right that kindness isn't a system, but neither is a rotation that resets our physical comfort every few months. Let's just be honest about the noise and ergonomics and assign the seats. I'm voting B.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree with everyone. Option B allows us to be mindful of each other's needs while keeping our team's heart beating strong. I will vote for Option B to ensure we stay connected and stable.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is the only logical choice for the budget and the physical requirements of the room. As long as we commit to a transparent assignment of the less desirable seats, I will vote for B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think you're all right. If we can be fair about the seats and keep the costs low, it's the best way. I'll vote for Option B too.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm so glad we all agree! No more cable chaos or endless boxes for me. I'm voting for Option B to keep our days smooth and stress-free!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"It's rare we're all on the same page, but the data makes it inevitable. Stability is the only way to manage the noise and the ergonomics without losing our minds. I'm voting B.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
